{"object":"Metal contacts can be protected against oxidation, processors debounce contact oscillation, and hot-swap sockets let switches be replaced without normal soldering. These generic mechanisms describe switch and socket boundaries; they do not establish a complete keyboard's lifetime or make its PCB replaceable.","predicate":"bound","source_url":"http://localhost:8090/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic/Keyboard_technology","subject":"keyboard switch and hot-swap mechanisms","text":"Keyboard mechanisms explain metal-contact oxidation protection, debounce, and switch replacement through hot-swap sockets, but none of those generic facts proves whole-board longevity or PCB serviceability.","title":"prop_keyboard_component_mechanisms"}